log
@TPV, SIP, and if possible, the general Polynomial distortion function are
now implemented by the Template Polynomial Distortion (TPD), that being a
superset of TPV and SIP.  TPD, also handles 1D distortions and can be used
for inversions.  TPD efficiently handles 1D distortions and distortions
without radial terms, and is supported as a separate distortion type
defined by Paper IV keywords.  New functions: tpdset(), sipset(), and
pol2tpd().  All of the old tpv*() functions now become tpd*().
